# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a pull request into main (needs branch protection with
# "Require review from Code Owners", see guides/deploy.md). Later lines win over earlier ones.
# In this public repository every path is owned by @Kissofbeauty. Forks / organization copies:
# split the owners as intended — system paths below to your sysadmin team (e.g. @your-org/sysadmins)
# and /Organization-Knowledge/ to your content owners (e.g. @your-org/hr); teams need write access.

# Default: everything not listed below
*                           @Kissofbeauty

# Content owners (HR, Security, Marketing, department heads) may change knowledge and KPI
# (fork: your content-owners team)
/Organization-Knowledge/    @Kissofbeauty

# Skills are instructions every agent follows — they act like code (security review M-06), so the
# sysadmin team must approve every Skills change. This line comes later and wins for Skills/ folders:
# only the sysadmin team is the code owner there. Content owners still review the wording: the
# pull request template asks for it and CI (job skills-review) flags every Skills change, with the
# links and shell blocks in it. To REQUIRE both teams, also add a ruleset/branch rule with 2 approvals.
# (fork: your sysadmin team, e.g. @your-org/sysadmins)
/Organization-Knowledge/**/Skills/   @Kissofbeauty

# System settings and anything that runs on the server: sysadmin approval only (fork: your sysadmin team)
/Config/ohermes.conf        @Kissofbeauty
/ohermes                    @Kissofbeauty
/Config/                    @Kissofbeauty
/Infrastructure/            @Kissofbeauty
/docker-compose.yml         @Kissofbeauty
/Users/_template/           @Kissofbeauty
/.github/                   @Kissofbeauty
/.env.example               @Kissofbeauty
